All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed in `src/`:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: Added case-insensitive comparison using `.lower()` on both the required role and each user role.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: Changed `and` to `or` so that being either an admin *or* the owner grants access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: Replaced the mutable default argument `={}` with `| None = None` and copied the input with `dict(initial)` to prevent shared state across instances.
- `add`: Changed `self._stock[sku] = qty` to `+=` so repeated adds accumulate.
- `reserve`: Changed `qty >= available` to `qty > available` so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed.
- `release`: Added a guard raising `ValueError` when the release quantity exceeds the currently reserved amount.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: Lowercased alphanumeric characters and replaced the single `replace("--", "-")` with a `while` loop that fully collapses repeated separators.
- `truncate`: Shortened the kept prefix to `max_len - len(suffix)` so the total result length never exceeds `max_len`.
